WEBVTT

00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:06.208
This guide brings the drainage checks, supporting
sources and assessment record together.

00:00:06.228 --> 00:00:11.394
We’ll work through an example housing application:
find the relevant guidance, check the

00:00:11.414 --> 00:00:14.814
submission, request missing evidence and record the
next review.

00:00:14.834 --> 00:00:19.261
The application and documents in this demonstration
are fictional.

00:00:19.281 --> 00:00:23.063
You can jump to any stage using the chapters below
the video.

00:00:23.083 --> 00:00:27.788
If you are unsure where to start, open Find guidance
for a proposal.

00:00:27.808 --> 00:00:33.752
Choose the application stage, discharge destination,
drainage features and known constraints.

00:00:34.432 --> 00:00:38.837
Here, we have a non-major full application proposing
infiltration.

00:00:38.857 --> 00:00:42.494
The result gives us a starting sequence and relevant
checks.

00:00:42.514 --> 00:00:47.002
Open the application checklist for the evidence
expected at that stage.

00:00:47.022 --> 00:00:52.524
The route helps you prioritise; the full set of
assessment checks remains available.

00:00:52.544 --> 00:00:58.373
Open Assess an application. Enter the application
reference and type, then open the

00:00:58.393 --> 00:01:02.490
record. A saved assessment can be reopened from this
page.

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:07.460
Each job has its own record, and each revised
submission has its own review

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:11.853
round. We’ll use the sections across the top to work
from the site through

00:01:11.873 --> 00:01:17.543
to the consultation response. Browser saving is
local: export a copy for the case

00:01:17.563 --> 00:01:20.353
file. Start with Site and constraints.

00:01:20.373 --> 00:01:23.797
Enter the proposal and a site grid reference.

00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:28.779
The postcode lookup can give you an approximate
starting location; check it against the

00:01:28.799 --> 00:01:34.043
actual site. Open the relevant maps and record the
result, source and date for

00:01:34.063 --> 00:01:38.727
each constraint. Some links centre on the location;
others open a report list or

00:01:38.747 --> 00:01:43.982
a separate service. Follow the related-check links
to see what a constraint affects.

00:01:44.002 --> 00:01:47.450
A map link does not record its answer for you.

00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:52.059
In Key numbers, name the documents and revisions,
then enter their figures in the

00:01:52.079 --> 00:01:56.445
correct units. Add another document when you need a
comparison.

00:01:56.465 --> 00:02:00.535
Our strategy and calculation sheet give different
impermeable areas.

00:02:00.555 --> 00:02:05.455
The flag draws attention to that disagreement and
links to the relevant checks.

00:02:05.475 --> 00:02:09.417
Confirm the reason in the original documents and
record your finding.

00:02:09.437 --> 00:02:14.061
A number with no flag still needs to be checked
against the design and

00:02:14.081 --> 00:02:19.588
its assumptions. Now open Checks and record the
documents, revisions and review date.

00:02:19.608 --> 00:02:24.053
Use the topics and outcome filter to work through
the submission.

00:02:24.073 --> 00:02:29.337
The labels distinguish requirements, conditional
requirements, Torbay criteria, recommendations

00:02:29.357 --> 00:02:33.637
and officer guidance. Read when each check applies.

00:02:34.437 --> 00:02:37.978
For our infiltration proposal, open IG-02.

00:02:37.998 --> 00:02:42.567
Read What to check, Evidence to look for and Gap to
check.

00:02:42.587 --> 00:02:47.889
Read source wording opens the original wording and
references beside the check, with evidence

00:02:47.909 --> 00:02:53.095
and examples where available. Our report gives a
test result but omits the test

00:02:53.115 --> 00:02:56.616
location and depth. Choose More information needed.

00:02:56.636 --> 00:03:02.198
In the finding, name the document, revision and
page, then explain what is missing.

00:03:02.798 --> 00:03:05.852
Use Not applicable only with a recorded reason.

00:03:05.872 --> 00:03:11.886
The summary keeps missing evidence, unmet criteria,
alternatives and unreviewed checks

00:03:11.906 --> 00:03:17.097
visible. You can also upload published or anonymised
PDF and Word reports.

00:03:17.117 --> 00:03:22.202
Check the report titles and revisions, confirm that
the documents may be used, and

00:03:22.222 --> 00:03:27.740
inspect the extracted text. Drawings, scans and
anything the extraction misses still need

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:33.411
a manual check. Prepare preliminary review shows the
request allowance before you start.

00:03:33.431 --> 00:03:38.567
Open a preliminary finding, read its quoted evidence
and follow the linked guidance.

00:03:38.587 --> 00:03:44.052
Edit the finding, choose the outcome yourself and
accept it into the matching assessment.

00:03:44.072 --> 00:03:47.771
Work through the remaining findings in the same way.

00:03:47.791 --> 00:03:50.813
For a focused question, open the guidance chat.

00:03:50.833 --> 00:03:55.157
Choose guidance only, or the relevant uploaded
evidence.

00:03:55.177 --> 00:03:58.549
Ask what is needed to support the infiltration test.

00:03:58.569 --> 00:04:03.762
Follow the answer’s references and check the
original evidence before relying on it.

00:04:03.782 --> 00:04:06.641
The panel can stay open alongside the page.

00:04:07.241 --> 00:04:12.200
In Summary and conclusion, review the outstanding
findings and write the next action.

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:17.898
Then open Request information. Select the findings
to include and choose

00:04:17.918 --> 00:04:23.482
Prepare selected paragraphs. Each paragraph can be
edited, reordered or removed.

00:04:23.502 --> 00:04:28.881
Make the request specific to the submission: here,
we need a plan locating the

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:31.923
infiltration tests, their depths and the supporting
test records.

00:04:32.723 --> 00:04:37.754
Read the complete wording, then copy the request
into the council’s normal correspondence

00:04:37.774 --> 00:04:42.977
process. When that review round is finished,
complete it to preserve its findings and

00:04:42.997 --> 00:04:48.223
documents. Start revised submission, enter the new
references and review date, and open

00:04:48.243 --> 00:04:52.287
the next round. Return to the outstanding check.

00:04:52.307 --> 00:04:54.918
The original finding is retained.

00:04:54.938 --> 00:05:00.052
Record the applicant’s response and revised evidence
reference, then assess the new evidence

00:05:00.072 --> 00:05:05.507
and record the outcome. Other findings may carry
forward, but recheck anything affected

00:05:05.527 --> 00:05:10.246
by the revised design. Earlier rounds lets you read
the history.

00:05:10.266 --> 00:05:15.714
In this example, the test-location query is
answered, but the wider testing evidence still

00:05:15.734 --> 00:05:20.276
needs checking. The separate area discrepancy
remains outstanding.

00:05:20.296 --> 00:05:25.767
Open Consultation response and choose the
recommendation supported by your review.

00:05:25.787 --> 00:05:29.003
Our remaining discrepancy calls for further
information.

00:05:29.023 --> 00:05:34.694
Check the reasons and information required, and edit
them to match the current findings.

00:05:34.714 --> 00:05:38.805
Add suitable conditions or informatives only where
they are appropriate.

00:05:38.825 --> 00:05:43.551
Enter the officer details, read the assembled
response, then copy it or use Print

00:05:43.571 --> 00:05:46.326
response to save the finished document as a PDF.

00:05:47.646 --> 00:05:50.582
Open the saved document and check it before issue.

00:05:50.602 --> 00:05:54.810
Recording a recommendation here does not send it to
the planning system.

00:05:54.830 --> 00:06:00.467
Export record creates a file for reopening the
assessment, containing the findings,

00:06:00.487 --> 00:06:03.127
requests, completed rounds and assessment basis.

00:06:03.887 --> 00:06:06.549
Download it and keep it with the case file.

00:06:06.569 --> 00:06:11.447
To continue elsewhere, use Import a record and
select that exported file.

00:06:12.007 --> 00:06:15.256
Check the application reference and round when it
opens.

00:06:15.276 --> 00:06:17.753
You can also print the assessment.

00:06:17.773 --> 00:06:22.468
If the guide flags a change in its source basis,
recheck the affected finding

00:06:22.488 --> 00:06:25.462
before recording that the change has been reviewed.

00:06:25.482 --> 00:06:30.085
For a quick query, search by rule code, subject or a
phrase, and narrow

00:06:30.105 --> 00:06:35.858
the results when needed. Rules and guidance provides
the searchable register, topic pages

00:06:35.878 --> 00:06:41.614
and proposal route. Read the original sources when
the wording or status matters.

00:06:41.634 --> 00:06:47.410
Check a number brings together runoff comparisons,
rainfall allowances, infiltration factors

00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:53.089
and interception criteria. Follow the units and
assumptions shown beside each tool.

00:06:53.109 --> 00:06:57.989
Site maps and Key numbers also work without an
application; save those details to

00:06:58.009 --> 00:07:00.696
a new assessment when you are ready.

00:07:00.716 --> 00:07:05.370
SuDS features connects component design and
maintenance guidance to the relevant checks.

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:10.892
Review aids contains evidence guides, decision
guides and published examples.

00:07:10.912 --> 00:07:16.125
Sources shows the document versions; Torbay local
criteria explains the local context,

00:07:16.145 --> 00:07:20.736
and the glossary and other-permissions pages help
with specific questions.

00:07:20.756 --> 00:07:25.396
The working sequence is the same: find the check,
verify the evidence, record your

00:07:25.416 --> 00:07:28.171
reasoning and keep the review history with the job.

